int  main(void)
{
  return (0);
}
不准备从command line接手argument

但考试中write a program that takes a string as an argument
需要接收从terminal传来的东西
int  main(int argc, char **argv)
{
  return (0);
}

argc, argument count: command line一共有多少个argument
比如：
terminal运行./a.out
此时argc = 1
program自己的名字也算一个argument
./a.out Hello的话：argc = 2

argv, argument vector: 一个装着command line arguments的array
./a.out Hello Cat
argv
argv[0] "./a.out"
argv[1] "Hello"
argv[2] "Cat"
argc = 3

int tab[i]里的element是int
argv[]里的element是string

./a.out Hello Cat
argv[1][0] = 'H'
argv[1][1] = 'e'
argv[1][2] = 'l'
argv[1][3] = 'l'
argv[1][4] = 'o'
argv[1][5] = '\0'

char **argv可以让我访问多个strings
argv[i] -> 一个string / char *
argv[i] -> 这个string里的一个char

Example quiz
Write a program that takes a string as an argument and displays the first 'a' character it encounters, followed by a newline.
If there are no 'a' characters, display 'a' followed by a newline.
If the number of parameters is not exactly 1, display 'a' followed by a newline.

takes a string as an argument
所以不应该是int s，而是argv[1]
比如./a.out Hello Cat里，我们把"Hello"当作一个argument
Shell中的quotes不会进入argument，所以如果是./a.out Hello "Cat 1"，那么"Cat 1"的双引号不会进入argument
但是"Cat 1"里的空格算作真的character

注意
'P' 这是character，字符
"P" 这是string
string都是从[0]开始算起的

#include <unistd.h>

int  main(int argc, char **argv)
{
  ...
  return (0);
}

#include <unistd.h>
int  main(void)
{
  write(1, "a\n", 2);
  return (0);
}

修改题目为：
Write a program.
Take one string as argument and display the string itself, followed by newline.
If the number of arguments is not exactly 1, display only newline.

举例：
./a.out Piscine
→ Piscine

./a.out "Hello Cat"
→ Hello Cat

./a.out
→ [newline]

./a.out Hello Cat
→ [newline]

那么：
int  main(int argc, char **argv)
{
  int  i;

  i = 0;
  if (argc != 2)
  {
    write(1, "/n", 1);
  }
  else
  {
    while (argv[1][i] != '\0')
    {
      write(1, &argv[1][i], 1);
      i++;
    }
    write(1, "/n", 1);
  }
  return (0);
}


------------

if (argc == 2)
{
  while (argv[1][i] != '\0')
  {
      write(1, &argv[1][i], 1);
      i++;
  }
}
write(1, "\n", 1);
return (0);

------------
Blind Test：first_char
写一个program：
Write a program that takes exactly one string as an argument and displays the first character of the string, followed by a newline.
If the number of arguments is not exactly 1, the program displays only a newline.

Allowed function: write
例如：
./a.out Piscine
输出P

#include <unistd.h>

int  main(int argc, char **argv)
{
  if (argc == 2)
  {
    write(1, &argv[1][0], 1);
  }
  write(1, "\n", 1);
  return (0);
}

